                ✔ CHANGE: Commit button now hold-to-confirm, not click @done(26-08-14) (found
                   during the same solo smoke-test: committing consumed the docked relics on a
                   single right-click, same as every other Forge interactable — but Commit is the
                   one action that's IRREVERSIBLE, so an accidental click there is a real loss, not
                   a redo. Now uses the same hold-to-confirm mechanism vanilla uses for module
                   deconstruction (ExtruderLever/HoldClickerInteractable, driven by the F/Hold
                   action) instead of the Forge's usual click path (CarryableInteract's fire1Action,
                   right-click in this game's bindings).
                   New ForgeCommitInteractable : HoldClickerInteractable — NOT a ForgeInteractable,
                   because ClickerInteractable is a sibling branch off AbstractInteractable, not a
                   base ForgeInteractable shares, so the two can't be unified. Dispatched through
                   EnvironmentInteract (vanilla's always-on Ability for the Hold/interact key), a
                   completely separate pathway from the Harmony prefix on CarryableInteract the rest
                   of the Forge uses — ZERO new patches needed, vanilla routes it for free once the
                   right component type sits on the collider. A stray fire1Action/right-click on it
                   now falls through to vanilla CarryableInteract.StartInteraction as a harmless
                   no-op (confirmed by reading the decompiled method: non-Grabbable/non-Socket
                   targets are ignored when empty-handed).
                   Two landmines from building a ClickerInteractable-derived type at runtime with no
                   prefab-authored Inspector data (same constraint every Forge interactable already
                   lives under): DontSelfSetInteractionInfo must be set before Start() runs
                   SetClickable(), or ClickerInteractable.Start() stomps the InteractionInfo
                   assignment back to the null it captured in Awake(); and Highlighted() is
                   overridden to skip ClickerInteractable's own version entirely, which iterates an
                   `outlineObjects` array nothing ever populates outside the Inspector (would NRE).
                   HandleInteraction/DescribeClick/Apply on UpgradeForgeBehavior were re-typed from
                   `ForgeInteractable target` to `(ForgeInteractableKind kind, Transform anchor)` so
                   both dispatch paths can share the one ForgeInteractionPolicy decision pipeline —
                   commit still only fires empty-handed, same as before, no policy changes. Hot-reload
                   teardown in Plugins.cs extended to sweep ForgeCommitInteractable too (separate
                   component type from ForgeInteractable, same generated-vs-authored-collider rule),
                   since a self-subscribed HoldCompleted handler on an orphaned instance would
                   otherwise leak silently across reloads.
