                 FOLLOW-UP (user, same session): the Commit prompt icon shows a mouse-click glyph
                 instead of a keyboard-key glyph (e.g. "F"), even though InteractionType was already
                 set to Hold.
                    ROOT CAUSE: KeyBindVE.Init resolves the icon by taking
                    InteractionDescription.Key.FallBackString, stripping "<keybind>...</keybind>" tags,
                    and looking THAT UP BY NAME as a live InputAction (InputService.FindActionKey — a
                    real search through InputActionAsset.actionMaps) — it's an action-name lookup, not
                    just a display label. ForgeInteractable.ActionInfo was borrowing source.Key from
                    _insertInfo (vanilla's regular click/interact InteractionInfo, borrowed from
                    CarryablesSocketActor) for EVERY prompt including Commit/Deconstruct — but Commit
                    and Deconstruct are actually driven by HoldClickerInteractable's own, SEPARATE
                    InputActionReferences.HoldAction (see that class) — a different bound input than the
                    click action. So the icon KeyBindVE resolved and showed was the CLICK action's glyph
                    (a mouse button in this control scheme), regardless of InteractionType already saying
                    Hold — InteractionType and the icon glyph are two independent things fed by two
                    different fields (InteractionType vs Key).
                    FIXED: ActionInfo now builds Key fresh for Hold-type prompts specifically, reading
                    the Hold action's own live name off
                    ServiceBase<InputService>.Instance.InputActionReferences.HoldAction.action.name
                    (not hardcoded, so a future rebind/rename in the Input Actions asset can't silently
                    desync this from what HoldClickerInteractable itself listens on) and wrapping it in
                    the same "<keybind>ActionName</keybind>" format vanilla's own Hold prompts use
                    (confirmed pattern: ContextInfoDisplay.cs:90 does
                    CreateInteraction(Hold, "<keybind>Fire1</keybind>", ...) for the vanilla Use prompt).
                    Non-Hold prompts (RelicTube/ModuleSocket/AlloyTerminal) are untouched — still borrow
                    _insertInfo's Key as before, which is correct for them (Press-type, same click action).
                    Also added a LogDebug reporting the resolved action name for every Hold prompt built,
